$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-stock-decryption
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
<meta name="twitter:site" content="@MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:url" content="https\://maizegdb.org/stock_decryption">
<meta property="og:title" content="Reading a seed packet | MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:description" content="What the handwriting on a Maize Genetics Cooperation Stock Center seed packet means: the stock number, the pedigree, the parents' genotypes and the kernel count.">

<a class="mgdb-skip-link" href="#sd-main">Skip to main content</a>

<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-packet-page" id="sd-main">

  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
    <a href="/data_center/stock">Stocks</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
    <span aria-current="page">Reading a seed packet</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero" aria-labelledby="sd-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem sd-emblem">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 96 96" role="img" aria-label="A seed packet with four lines of writing on it">
        <rect x="24" y="10" width="48" height="76" rx="4" fill="#fdf3cf" stroke="#235c37" stroke-width="3" />
        <path d="M24 22h48" stroke="#235c37" stroke-width="2" />
        <path d="M32 34h20 M32 42h32" stroke="#8a6a2f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <path d="M34 54h28" stroke="#8a6a2f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <path d="M34 60h20" stroke="#d99a0b" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <path d="M32 74h12" stroke="#8a6a2f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
      </svg>
      <strong>Seed packet</strong>
      <span class="sd-emblem-meta">A &middot; B &middot; C &middot; D</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="sd-title">Reading a Stock Center seed packet</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">Seed from the Maize Genetics Cooperation Stock Center arrives in a paper packet with four things written on it by hand: which stock it is, where in the nursery it was grown, what its parents were, and how many kernels are inside. This page reads one real packet line by line.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
    <a href="#sd-packet" class="is-current" aria-current="true">The packet</a>
    <a href="#sd-parts">What each part means</a>
    <a href="#sd-notation">Notation reference</a>
    <a href="#sd-related">Related resources</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="sd-packet" aria-labelledby="sd-packet-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="sd-packet-title">The packet</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="sd-lead">A real packet, of Stock Center stock <a href="/data_center/stock?id=14067">222B</a>. The four lettered regions are explained below &mdash; select one on the packet to jump to it.</p>

    <div class="sd-packet-layout">
      <figure class="sd-packet">
        <div class="sd-packet-media">
          <img src="/images/SeedPacket.jpg" width="402" height="661" decoding="async"
               alt="A yellow paper seed packet with four groups of handwriting, each marked with a letter. A, at the top left: 222B on the first line and TB-3La-2S(6270&#41; on the second. B, in the upper middle: 96-750-11 written above a horizontal line with 749-1 below it. C, in the lower middle: TB over N, then a slash, then W23 over L317. D, at the bottom left: 20k.">
          <a class="sd-region sd-region-a" href="#sd-a"><span class="mgdb-visually-hidden">Region A: stock number and focus genotype</span></a>
          <a class="sd-region sd-region-b" href="#sd-b"><span class="mgdb-visually-hidden">Region B: pedigree</span></a>
          <a class="sd-region sd-region-c" href="#sd-c"><span class="mgdb-visually-hidden">Region C: genotypes of the parents</span></a>
          <a class="sd-region sd-region-d" href="#sd-d"><span class="mgdb-visually-hidden">Region D: number of kernels</span></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Photographed at the Maize Genetics Cooperation Stock Center. The lettering is ours; the handwriting is the Stock Center's.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="sd-key">
        <h3>What is written where</h3>
        <dl class="sd-key-list">
          <div>
            <dt><span class="sd-key-tag">A</span> Stock number and focus genotype</dt>
            <dd><code>222B</code> and <code>TB-3La-2S&#40;6270&#41;</code> &mdash; which stock this is, and the feature it is kept for. <a href="#sd-a">Read on</a></dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt><span class="sd-key-tag">B</span> Pedigree</dt>
            <dd><code>96-750-11</code> over <code>749-1</code> &mdash; year, row and plant, female parent over male. <a href="#sd-b">Read on</a></dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt><span class="sd-key-tag">C</span> Genotypes of the parents</dt>
            <dd><code>TB/N</code> and <code>W23/L317</code> &mdash; female genotype, then a slash, then male. <a href="#sd-c">Read on</a></dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt><span class="sd-key-tag">D</span> Kernels in the packet</dt>
            <dd><code>20k</code> &mdash; twenty kernels. <a href="#sd-d">Read on</a></dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="sd-parts" aria-labelledby="sd-parts-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="sd-parts-title">What each part means</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="sd-part" id="sd-a">
      <h3><span class="sd-key-tag">A</span> Stock number and focus genotype</h3>
      <div class="sd-prose">
        <p>The top left identifier is the Stock Center's own stock number, followed by the focus genotype or some other feature of interest. On this packet those are <strong>222B</strong> and <strong>TB-3La-2S&#40;6270&#41;</strong>, a B-A translocation.</p>
        <p>Both are records at MaizeGDB. The enlargements below are from this packet, and each one links to the record it names.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="sd-crops">
        <a class="sd-crop" href="/data_center/stock?id=14067">
          <img src="/images/A_top.jpg" width="136" height="67" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="The handwritten stock number 222B, enlarged from the packet.">
          <span><strong>222B</strong>Stock record <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>
        <a class="sd-crop" href="/data_center/variation?id=15217">
          <img src="/images/A_bottom.jpg" width="307" height="69" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="The handwritten genotype TB-3La-2S(6270&#41;, enlarged from the packet.">
          <span><strong>TB-3La-2S&#40;6270&#41;</strong>Variation record <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sd-part" id="sd-b">
      <h3><span class="sd-key-tag">B</span> Pedigree</h3>
      <div class="sd-prose">
        <p>Next is the pedigree: a set of numbers like <code>96-750-11</code>, meaning the seed was harvested in <strong>1996</strong> from <strong>row 750</strong>, <strong>plant 11</strong>.</p>
        <p>When that identifier sits above a line with a second set of numbers below it, the seed is the result of a cross: <strong>the female parent is above the line and the male parent below</strong>. This packet reads <code>96-750-11</code> over <code>749-1</code>.</p>
        <p>A letter after the year part marks a winter nursery &mdash; P for Puerto Rico, H for Hawaii, GH for greenhouse. A male parent written <code>S-#</code> means a sib cross. A circled X, sometimes written <code>@</code>, means a self pollination. All of these are collected in the <a href="#sd-notation">notation reference</a> below.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sd-part" id="sd-c">
      <h3><span class="sd-key-tag">C</span> Genotypes of the parents</h3>
      <div class="sd-prose">
        <p>The genotype of the female parent is listed, then a slash, then the genotype of the male parent. This packet reads <code>TB/N</code>&nbsp;/&nbsp;<code>W23/L317</code>.</p>
        <p>Where <strong>both an upper and a lower case letter</strong> appear for a parent, that parent is a <strong>heterozygote</strong>. Where only one or the other appears, the parent was <strong>homozygous</strong> for the allele listed. Introgression into a defined inbred background is sometimes noted here too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sd-part" id="sd-d">
      <h3><span class="sd-key-tag">D</span> Kernels in the packet</h3>
      <div class="sd-prose">
        <p>The number of seeds &#40;kernels&#41; in the packet. <code>20k</code> is twenty kernels.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="sd-notation" aria-labelledby="sd-notation-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="sd-notation-title">Notation reference</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="sd-lead">Every symbol the sections above describe, in one place.</p>

    <div class="mgdb-table-scroll">
      <table class="mgdb-table sd-notation-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Written</th>
            <th scope="col">Means</th>
            <th scope="col">Where</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>96-750-11</code></th>
            <td>Year, row, plant &mdash; harvested in 1996 from row 750, plant 11.</td>
            <td>B</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>one line over another</code></th>
            <td>A cross. Female parent above the line, male parent below.</td>
            <td>B</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>96<strong>P</strong>-750-11</code></th>
            <td>A letter after the year marks a winter nursery. P is Puerto Rico, H is Hawaii, GH is greenhouse.</td>
            <td>B</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>S-#</code></th>
            <td>As the male parent, a sib cross.</td>
            <td>B</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">a circled X, or <code>@</code></th>
            <td>A self pollination.</td>
            <td>B</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>female / male</code></th>
            <td>The slash separates the two parents' genotypes, female first.</td>
            <td>C</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>A/a</code></th>
            <td>Both an upper and a lower case letter&#58; that parent is a heterozygote.</td>
            <td>C</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>A</code> or <code>a</code> alone</th>
            <td>Only one case shown&#58; that parent was homozygous for the allele listed.</td>
            <td>C</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><code>20k</code></th>
            <td>The number of kernels in the packet.</td>
            <td>D</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-note" role="note">
      <strong>Allele names are written the same way everywhere.</strong> The upper and lower case convention on the packet is the standard maize convention, not a Stock Center shorthand&#58; see <a href="/nomenclature">maize genetics nomenclature</a> for how gene, allele and stock names are formed.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="sd-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="sd-related-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="sd-related-title">Related resources</h2></div>
    </div>

